# AI Quality Control

## Objective

AI-generated work must meet the same bar as human work  -  accurate, scoped, and verifiable.

## Requirements

- Verify file paths, APIs, and dependencies exist before using them (`anti-hallucination.mdc`).
- Follow all `alwaysApply` rules in `.cursor/rules/`.
- Prefer small, reviewable diffs.
- State uncertainty explicitly; investigate instead of guessing (`uncertainty-handling.mdc`).
- Self-review every change (`self-review.mdc`).

## Subagents and Delegation

When delegating, inject project rules into subagent prompts. Parent orchestrates; subagents must not expand scope silently.

## Golden Rule

AI output is a draft until evidence and review say otherwise.